/* Clock elements (docs/ui/AUTHORING.md "Clock elements"). The NovaUI runtime
   registers them; their clock is nui.now(), so a time a controller writes
   into a model is nui.now() plus seconds.

   <nui-countdown format="dhms" day="@game.DAY" hour="@game.HOUR" minute="@game.MINUTE"
   	second="@game.SECOND" data-attr-end="icon.end"/>
   	the remaining time as text, changed at most once a second; format="none"
   	is a timer that only sends countdownend.
   <nui-cooldown data-attr-start="slot.cd_start" data-attr-end="slot.cd_end"/>
   	a cooldown sweep: the remaining part of [start, end), counter-clockwise
   	from the top as the legacy box draws it, in 64 steps; hidden outside
   	its span.

   The sweep is a progress element: RmlUi builds its circular geometry only
   from a fill-image, which it resolves against the document, so the image
   is a store path (a white texel tinted by image-color). The sweep covers
   its positioned parent's box; a component that places it inside a part of
   that box (the slot grid) sets its own left, top and size. */

nui-countdown
{
	display: inline;
}

nui-cooldown
{
	display: block;
	position: absolute;
	left: 0;
	top: 0;
	right: 0;
	bottom: 0;
	fill-image: /nui/components/img/solid.tga;
	image-color: var(--cooldown-shade);
	pointer-events: none;
}
